# PEPTIDE INTELLIGENCE

This workspace is an evidence engine for peptides and GLP-1s — not a catalog and not a clinic.

## Evidence labels (required)

Label claims as: FACT | INFERENCE | EXPERT OPINION | ANIMAL DATA | ANECDOTE | MARKETING CLAIM | UNKNOWN.

## Hard rules

1. Regulators and RCTs first; forums last.
2. Animal work stays in its own box — never presented as human proof.
3. PCAC votes are advisory only — not compounding authorization, not FDA approval.
4. A COA is not sterility. Study doses are research context, not patient doses.
5. Two peptides studied separately are not a studied stack — do not invent synergy.
6. Do not write personal protocols, prescriptions, or individualized dosing.
7. Do not treat research-chemical / “not for human use” websites as a medical supply chain.
8. Non-peptides in peptide culture get: COMMUNITY PEPTIDE — TECHNICALLY NOT A PEPTIDE.
9. Scores are not inflated for fame.

## Regulatory freeze line (2026-09-07)

- Shortage compounding for semaglutide/tirzepatide has ended.
- July 2026 PCAC recommended six peptides for possible 503A listing; they are NOT lawful 503A bulks until FDA rulemaking.
- WADA bans: BPC-157 (S0), TB-500 (S2.3), many GH-axis peptides (S2.2.x).

